  <prompt>
    Make the exported Word comments mirror the on-screen gutter. Today each w:comment bakes the RAW explanation prose +
    a hardcoded author. Build the export mirror: configurable AUTHOR (prop/config, not the literal at
    ComposeEditor.tsx:2146) · "Flagged clause" label (not "Grounded fact") · "Assessment says: …" · "Standard: …"
    (citation; full clause text when available). With 002's discrete fields there is NOTHING to string-parse — compose
    the structured export text from flaggedClause/assessment/standardRef. Server ApplyComment needs NO change.
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Compose comment-thread export mapping, docx save flow.</role>
  <goal>A saved-then-opened-in-Word agreement shows structured comments identical in content to the gutter; author configurable.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Root cause (notes/word-comment-export-gap.md — one cause, four symptoms): the relabel exists ONLY in the gutter
      (ComposeCommentGutter.tsx:343-378 display-only); export reads only author/text/timestamp
      (composeSessionCommentThreadsToAnchoredComments, ComposeCommentThread.types.ts:256-262) and standardRef is
      explicitly dropped (never-export scope at :89 — lift it deliberately, documenting the decision); author hardcoded
      at ComposeEditor.tsx:2146 (useComposeCommentThreads(editor,'AI Advisory Review')). Two candidate seams: compose the
      structured string at placeAdvisoryComments-time OR at the export mapping — the export-mapping seam keeps the
      thread's raw fields intact for the UI; prefer it unless step-0 audit says otherwise. Post-002 threads carry
      discrete metadata; older threads (pre-split) may carry only explanation — degrade gracefully (export raw text).
      Line refs are pre-merge — re-locate. Also verify against 030-032: durable-recalled threads must export identically
      to live-placed ones.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeCommentThread.types.ts (export mapping + scope lift)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (author config)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1/notes/word-comment-export-gap.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs (ApplyComment — NO change)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">discrete flaggedClause/assessment fields</dependency>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">renamed files (same-file order)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Server ApplyComment unchanged — it renders whatever commentText/Author it is given; the fix is client-side export composition. Scope: whole task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The never-export scope lift (:89) is a deliberate decision — document it at the change site (why standardRef now exports). Scope: the mapping.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Export structure mirrors the GUTTER's labels exactly ("Flagged clause" / "Assessment says:" / "Standard:") — one relabel source shared between gutter + export, not two copies. Scope: label source.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Author configurability is a lib-level prop/config with the current literal as default; scope: the author fix.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Comment export fidelity</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
