  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A saved-then-opened-in-Word review shows per comment: configured author · "Flagged clause" · "Assessment says: …" · "Standard: …" — mirroring the gutter (manual + mapping test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">standardRef exports (citation; full clause text when the thread carries it); the scope-lift is documented at the change site.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The gutter and the export consume ONE shared relabel source (no duplicated label maps — grep proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Legacy threads (raw explanation only) export their text without crash or fabricated structure.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: server ApplyComment untouched (git diff proof); durable-recalled threads export identically to live ones.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

